    "sut_status": "completed",
    "sut_verified": true,
    "final_summary": "Located the affected path user1 -> leaf1 -> spine1/spine2 -> wan1 -> external1 and verified baseline connectivity was intact. Read wan1 and found the shaped WAN uplink on eth2 had only an HTB root qdisc visible, implicating missing or incorrect class policy on the actual bottleneck. Applied a narrow QoS repair only on wan1 eth2: rebuilt the HTB root and added an explicit business class with 8 mbit rate plus a filter matching traffic to 203.0.113.10. Public validation then passed: lab connectivity remained successful and the observed throughput test under contention passed at 65.612 Mbps, above the required minimum.",
